<instruction name="VSHA512MSG2">
 <copyright>Copyright (C) Intel Corporation. All Rights Reserved.</copyright>
 <shortdesc>Perform a Final Calculation for the Next Four SHA512 Message Qwords</shortdesc>
 <longdesc><para unique="1047509">
   <string>The VSHA512MSG2 instruction is one of the two SHA512 message scheduling instructions. The instruction performs the final calculation for the next four SHA512 message qwords.</string></para>
  <para unique="1047511">
   <string>See</string><string> </string><anchor id="message URL https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/FIPS/NIST.FIPS.180-4.pdf"/><underline><string>https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/FIPS/NIST.FIPS.180-4.pdf</string></underline><string> for more information on the SHA512 standard.</string></para>
  </longdesc>
 <subsection title="Flags Affected">
  <para unique="1047537">
   <string>None.</string></para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Intel C/C++ Compiler Intrinsic Equivalent">
  <programlisting><string>VSHA512MSG2 __m256i _mm256_sha512msg2_epi64 (__m256i __A, __m256i __B);</string><string>
</string></programlisting>
  </subsection>
